{"type":"text","timestamp":1789788863076,"sessionID":"ses_f48467e2bffejC2lfVdrXfzZn1","part":{"id":"prt_0b7bab42f001DyiJ9N7gJQ9OQd","messageID":"msg_0b7baa3e4001qOZKjKvGUawzrL","sessionID":"ses_f48467e2bffejC2lfVdrXfzZn1","type":"text","text":"The Redis scripts were checking only whether a lock existed, rather than whether its token matched the worker’s. This allowed stale workers to remove or overwrite a replacement owner’s lock. I’ve restored token checks and moved delayed-job promotion after retry ownership validation so rejected retries cannot emit events or change queue state. The administrative token-`0` bypass remains intact.","time":{"start":1789788861487,"end":1789788863073},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_025ae608f2cb2ebd016aae02bd798c87d1b5f174b416b697d0","phase":"commentary"}}}}
