{"type":"text","timestamp":1789789229152,"sessionID":"ses_f48467e2bffejC2lfVdrXfzZn1","part":{"id":"prt_0b7c0316e001q05MovHcRpyKw1","messageID":"msg_0b7c026eb001F5GZX5UdShvhQp","sessionID":"ses_f48467e2bffejC2lfVdrXfzZn1","type":"text","text":"Fixed the ownership regression in four Redis Lua source files.\n\n### Changes\n- Restored token matching in `src/commands/includes/removeLock.lua`. Stale completion, failure, immediate retry, and delayed retry now return the existing lock-mismatch error before modifying the job or its owner’s lock.\n- Restored token matching in `extendLock-2.lua` and `extendLocks-1.lua`, preventing stale workers from renewing or replacing another owner’s lock.\n- Moved delayed-job promotion in `retryJob-11.lua` after ownership validation, preventing rejected retries from changing queue state or emitting events.\n- Preserved missing-lock errors and the administrative token-`0` bypass.\n\nAdded `tests/ownership.redis.test.ts` with four recovered-job scenarios verifying rejection, preserved job fields/events/lock ownership, and successful renewal and completion by the replacement owner.\n\n### Verification\nUsing Node **24.21.0**:\n- `npm run build` — passed.\n- Requested seven-file regression command — **268 tests passed**.\n- New ownership regression suite — **4 tests passed**.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\nThe first regression-suite run reached the shell’s 120-second timeout; the rerun with a longer timeout passed in 125 seconds.","time":{"start":1789789221230,"end":1789789229150},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0458d654e955e6ef016aae04253f2c87d1a34c690f1890f294","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
